## 3. Submission Flows

### 3.1 New Fob Request

**What it does:** A new member (no existing account) requests their first fob.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Member: Select 'New fob'] --> B[Member: Enter personal details]
    B --> C[Member: Select credential type]
    C --> D[Member: Review and submit]
    D --> E{System: Payment required?}
    E -->|Yes| F[System: SUBMITTED with Stripe PaymentIntent]
    F --> F2[Member: Pay via embedded Stripe form]
    F2 --> G[Stripe webhook: AWAITING_APPROVAL]
    E -->|No| G
    G --> H[Approver: Review with access level + member flags]
    H -->|Approve| I[System: AWAITING_PROGRAMMING]
    H -->|Reject| J[REJECTED - can be reopened]
    I --> K[Programmer: Program fob + enter serial]
    K --> L{Config: Split pickup?}
    L -->|No| M[System: Auto-set pickup - AWAITING_PICKUP]
    L -->|Yes| N[Issuer: Set pickup location]
    N --> M
    M --> O[Issuer: Issue fob]
    O --> P[ISSUED - Credential record created]

    style P fill:#22c55e,color:#fff
    style J fill:#ef4444,color:#fff
```

**Key details:**
- Blocked if email already has a membership - directed to "Additional fob" instead
- When payment is required, the request stays at `SUBMITTED` with an inline payment form. The Stripe webhook transitions it directly to `AWAITING_APPROVAL` on successful payment.
- `AWAITING_PAYMENT` status is only reached via exemption rejection, not initial submission.
- On approval, the approver sets the access level and any officer/board/staff flags.
- On issuing, a `credentials` record is created with status `active`. Existing deactivated/returned credentials with the same type + serial are reassigned rather than duplicated.

