### 4.4 Refunds (Manual and Auto)

**What it does:** Refunds a payment through Stripe. Can be triggered manually or automatically.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Refund triggered] --> B{Trigger type}
    B -->|Manual - Admin| C[Admin clicks Refund with reason]
    B -->|Auto - Cancel/Reject| D[Request cancelled or rejected]
    D --> E{paidAt set AND not already refunded?}
    E -->|No| F[Skip refund]
    E -->|Yes| G[Auto-trigger Stripe refund]
    C --> G
    G --> H{Stripe API call}
    H -->|Success| I[Record refundedAt, refundReason, stripeRefundId]
    I --> J[Send paymentRefunded email to member]
    I --> K[Audit log entry]
    H -->|Failure| L[Log error]
    L --> M{Was auto?}
    M -->|Yes| N[Cancel/reject proceeds anyway]
    M -->|No| O[Return 502 to admin]

    style J fill:#22c55e,color:#fff
```

**Key details:**
- **Auto-refund:** Happens automatically when a paid request is cancelled or rejected. Fire-and-forget - Stripe failures don't block the state transition.
- **Manual refund:** Requires `refund` permission. Returns 502 if Stripe fails.
- **Notification:** The member always receives a `paymentRefunded` email, regardless of trigger.
- **Idempotency:** Already-refunded requests are not refunded again.

