### 5.4 Pickup and Issuing

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Request at AWAITING_PICKUP] --> B[Member arrives]
    B --> C{Request type}
    C -->|new / additional / replacement| D[Issuer: Click 'Mark Issued']
    C -->|return / change_type| E[Issuer: Click 'Mark Issued' or 'Mark Collected']
    E --> F[Collection confirm: Collected fob from member?]
    F --> G[ISSUE with collected: true]
    D --> H{Pending credential exists?}
    G --> H
    H -->|Yes - from swap/manual| I[Activate pending credential]
    H -->|No| J[Create new credential record]
    I --> K[Status: ACTIVE]
    J --> K
    K --> L[Record issuedAt, issuedBy]
    L --> M[Email: Credential issued - with attachments]
    M --> N[ISSUED]

    style N fill:#22c55e,color:#fff
```

**Key details:**
- On issue: owner = requester, access level = from membership, expiry = calculated at approval
- If a deactivated/returned credential with the same type + serial exists, it's reassigned (not duplicated)
- Email includes any documents configured in `issuedEmailAttachmentUrls` (by-laws, policies)
- **Collection confirm (return and change_type only).** These two types hand a fob back, so the single "Mark Issued" click is replaced by a confirm step listing the fob to collect. The admin request page and the queue popover both route through it, and `transitionRequest` rejects an ISSUE for these types unless `collected: true` is recorded. `new`, `additional` and lost/damaged replacements keep the single click.
- On a `return` the confirm moves the credential `deactivated` to `returned` (audit `action: "collected"`) and sends the return confirmation. A return creates and activates no credential.
- On a `change_type` the confirm activates the new credential as above and, in the same transaction, moves the old credential `active` to `returned` (audit `action: "exchanged"`) and sets `programmingRequired` on it so a programmer removes it from the access system.

